.venv/
__pycache__
.aip_traces/
.pytest_cache/

# Lab 7 DELIBERATE EXCEPTIONS to the defaults above.
#
# .aip_cache/ and .github/ are ordinarily ignored, but the CI regression gate
# (labs/lab7/gate.py) runs with AIP_OFFLINE=1 and replays the committed response
# cache. Without these files tracked, CI cannot run at all: every request is a
# CacheMiss. README.md (Part D) says "Commit the cache" for exactly this reason.
#
# The cache holds prompts and model responses for a teaching corpus of public
# insurance documents. It contains no secrets -- .env stays ignored.
#
# ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING HERE. In git the LAST matching pattern wins, so a
# negation written above the rule it overrides does nothing at all. These
# negations used to sit at the top of the file, above `.aip_cache/*.sqlite3` at
# the bottom -- so calls.sqlite3 was ignored anyway and `git ls-files .aip_cache`
# returned nothing. The gate had no cache to replay on a fresh clone and a green
# CI build proved nothing. Keep every `!` below the rule it negates.
!.aip_cache/
!.github/
!.github/workflows/
!.github/workflows/eval.yml

Test_by_self
.env
corpus_scaled
ans
zip/*

# The bulk of the cache, and the one file that must be committed.
#
# Only calls.sqlite3 is tracked, and only after scripts/prune_cache.py has cut it
# from 164 MB to ~1.3 MB by keeping the keys offline replay actually reads (the
# 45 golden answers, the Lab 4 judge calls, and the 45 query vectors). The raw
# store stays ignored: .aip_cache/chroma/ duplicates data/index/ at 100x the
# size, and any other sqlite written here is experiment scratch.
.aip_cache/chroma/*
.aip_cache/*.sqlite3

# Machine-specific wall clock from the gate. Deliberately untracked: replaying
# the golden set measures this machine's Python, not the system, and it moves
# every run. reports/gate_metrics.json keeps the reproducible metrics only.
reports/gate_timing.local.json